WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.720
A peek behind the curtain on Game of Thrones
will reveal a number of things that may surprise

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.860
even the show’s most die-hard fans, from
the special effects in play to the true-life

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.660
relationships of the cast and crew.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.200
These are some of the most intriguing set
images from the show’s production.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.699
While it should come as no surprise that the
real-life relationships between professional

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:23.130
actors rarely mirror the characters they portray,
it can still throw you for a loop to discover

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.580
bitter onscreen rivals are in fact super-great
buds.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:32.860
Such was the case with Pedro Pascal, who played
the fiery, doomed Oberyn Martell, and Hafþór

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.500
Júlíus Björnsson, who played his sworn
enemy, Ser Gregor Clegane.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.320
Their shocking duel in season 4 remains one
of the most memorable moments of the series.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.440
That's why this picture of the two actors
soaking up rays together seems so odd.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.640
But while the difference between their onscreen
and offscreen relationship may inspire a double

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:54.120
take or two, that contrast in their real-life
physiques is exactly how they were depicted

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.740
on the show, with Björnsson towering over
his svelte pal.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.680
Anyone who has ever spent time on a set knows
the important roles that stand-ins and stunt

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.360
doubles play.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.560
These individuals provide coverage for the
actors between, and sometimes even during,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.060
filming.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.660
Actress Emilia Clarke's stand-in and stunt
double, Rosie Mac, has received a good share

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.270
of media attention over the course of the
show's run, thanks in part to the backstage

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.860
photos she often posts on her social media
accounts.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:22.940
And you’ve got to admit: all these stand-ins
look so similar to the show's famous leads

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.160
that it's actually kinda difficult to tell
them apart at first glance.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.820
As important as the actors are in bringing
the world of Game of Thrones to life, so too

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:31.880
are the crew members.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.420
Naturally, a story this epic in scope and
length requires hundreds of professionals

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.040
working tirelessly at their craft.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:42.420
Among the most important of these crew members
is Deborah Riley, who serves as the series'

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.680
lead production designer.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.540
One of the reasons the show has caught on
with so many people is because it feels so

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.040
real.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.380
Of course, it feels so real because much of
it is: many of the grand locales are shot

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.680
on location, rather than on a stage or studio
backlot.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:00.020
But this illusion is further cemented by the
intricate, but subtle, set decoration and

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.290
design, which captures the viewer's attention
without being so dazzling as to distract from

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.960
the drama of the story or the performances
of the actors.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.951
"You understand the textures, you understand
the colors, you understand the palette, you

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.840
understand so many things about the culture
that you're trying to recreate."

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.280
Of course, not every locale that appears on
Game of Thrones is the real deal.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.860
Location filming isn't always an option, so
in order to achieve a believable replication,

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.140
the effects crew will alternate between real
and digital locations.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.080
This type of visual trickery is nothing new
in and of itself, and Hollywood movies have

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.820
long used painted backdrops as stand-ins for
practical scenery.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.980
But this seamless blending of outdoor filming
with mobile greenscreens is just one of the

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.980
modern era’s most impressive achievements
in the field of CGI.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.720
Given how unforgettable many of these large-scale
scenes have proven, it's fair to say that

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.360
the show's special effects team has perfected
this kind of digital enhancement.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.620
Sadly, not everything on Game of Thrones can
be done with practical effects.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.930
In fact, one of the questions fans of the
books asked when the series was first announced

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.680
was just how such an epic story could be realistically
adapted to the screen.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.140
This was of particular concern since television
wasn’t exactly known for grand spectacle

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:06.640
at the time.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:11.380
And foremost among their concerns was the
show's ability to bring Daenerys Targaryen’s

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:11.940
dragons to life.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.260
"I'm here to help.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.280
Don't eat the help."

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.580
Luckily, it turned out the showrunners knew
exactly what they were doing.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.520
As a result, they've given us arguably the
definitive screen dragons of the modern era.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.459
But for these fantastical creatures, practical
effects just weren't practical.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:35.790
And yes, this might all look a bit silly,
but it really goes to show just what CGI can

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:36.700
really do.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.820
It’s always pretty remarkable to see the
show's actors on location, battling against

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:42.340
the elements.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:47.040
Such is the case with this image posted to
Instagram by Carice van Houten, who plays

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.800
the sinister witch Melisandre.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.480
On the show, she's utterly unflappable.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.950
She can stoically weather her surroundings
no matter how harsh the conditions, thanks

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.820
to the power she's achieved through her practice
of the dark arts.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.580
In real life, however, van Houten is just
as susceptible to the cold as the rest of

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.580
us mere mortals.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:06.860
It just goes to show, being a successful actor
isn't always as glamorous as it's made out

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:07.360
to be.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.020
One thing that should come as no surprise
to fans of the show by now is the close bond

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.880
shared between various cast members.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.520
Considering how many characters have been
killed off during the story so far, you’ve

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.320
got to imagine those cast members have probably
gotten used to saying goodbye to one another...

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:25.300
which is why it's cool to see they still hang
out with veterans from earlier seasons, such

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.340
as Jason Momoa, who played the late, great
Khal Drogo.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.900
According to Momoa's Instagram account, he
met up with his Game of Thrones buds in Belfast

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.460
during filming for the final season.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.880
Of course, these pictures sparked plenty of
speculation that the once-and-future Aquaman

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.180
would be returning to the series in some capacity
during its final season.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.980
Whether that turns out to be the case or not,
it's still always nice to see old friends

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:46.880
keeping in touch.

